{title: House of the Rising Sun}
{subtitle: Traditional American Folk Song (Public Domain)}
{artist: Traditional}
{composer: Traditional}
{key: Am}
{time: 6/8}
{tempo: 90}
{capo: 0}

{comment: This is the traditional public-domain version. 
It does NOT use lyrics or arrangement from The Animals.}

{comment: Suggested picking pattern (arpeggio)}
{comment: | 5 - 3 - 2 - 1 - 2 - 3 |}

{define: Am base-fret 1 frets 0 0 2 2 1 0}
{define: C  base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 1 0}
{define: E  base-fret 1 frets 0 2 2 1 0 0}

{start_of_verse}
[Am]There is a house in [C]New Orleans
[Am]They call the Rising [E]Sun
[Am]It's been the ruin of [C]many poor girl
[Am]And me, oh [E]Lord, I'm [Am]one
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Optional instrumental break}
{comment: | Am | C | Am | E |}

{start_of_verse}
[Am]If I had listened to [C]what my mother said
[Am]I'd be at home to[E]day
[Am]But I was young and [C]foolish, oh Lord
[Am]Let a rambler [E]lead me [Am]astray
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[Am]Go tell my baby [C]sister
[Am]Never do like I have [E]done
[Am]To shun that house in [C]New Orleans
[Am]They call the [E]Rising [Am]Sun
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[Am]I'm going back to [C]New Orleans
[Am]My race is almost [E]run
[Am]I'm going back to [C]end my life
[Am]Beneath the [E]Rising [Am]Sun
{end_of_verse}

{comment: End with a slow arpeggio on Am}
